Article 3
The Implementation of Protection of Women and Children aims to: provide guidance to the Regency Government in planning policies and strategies for the Protection of Women and Children;
prevent the occurrence of all forms of Violence against Women and Children as well as violations of the rights of Women and Children;
protect and provide services to Women and Child Victims of Violence;
strengthen the protective environment for Women and Children from all forms of Violence, exploitation, abuse and neglect;
increase empowerment of Women and Children; and increase the role of government institutions, business entities, media and/or NGOs in the Region.

Article 8
families and parents have obligations and responsibilities toward Children in the form of: caring for, maintaining, educating, and protecting Children;
preventing the occurrence of marriage at an early age;
ensuring the continuity of Children's education in accordance with the Children's abilities, talents and interests; and reporting every birth of a Child to the authorized agency to conduct birth registration.
In the event that parents do not exist or their whereabouts are unknown or due to a certain reason, cannot carry out their obligations and responsibilities, then the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1) may be transferred to the family, which shall be implemented in accordance with the applicable laws and regulations.

Article 13
The Implementation of Protection of Women and Children includes:
a. 	prevention and Protection;
b. 	Handling, recovery of victims of Violence;
c. 	Rehabilitation, Reintegration and empowerment;
d. 	law enforcement services and legal assistance;
e. 	facilitation of Child justice; and
f. 	cultivation of a gender-equitable social system.

Article 6
The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to: respect and guarantee the human rights of every Woman and Child without distinguishing ethnicity, religion, race, group, gender, ethnic group, culture, and language, legal status of the Child, birth order of the Child, and physical and/or mental condition;
provide support for facilities and infrastructure in the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children, including providing breastfeeding places for Children, playgrounds, recreational places, shelters, as well as establishing integrated service centers for Protection of Women and Children;
supervise the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children;
guarantee the availability of a safe and comfortable environment for optimal Child growth and development;
allocate budget to Institutions that have programs in the field of Protection of Women and Children;
coordinate programs, budgets and services that guarantee ease of service to victims;
formulate guidelines for the implementation of Protection of Women and Children;
provide services for Women and Child Victims of Violence;
monitor, supervise and evaluate the Implementation of Protection and Assistance for Women and Children;
prevent, reduce risks, and carry out handling of all forms of Violence, exploitation, maltreatment, Children in conflict with the law and Children in emergency situations;
strengthen family-based and Community-based Child care;
increase Child participation in policy-making that affects them, including in family life, education and Community; and increase Community participation in the Protection of Women and Children including prevention, risk reduction and its handling.
The provision of facilities and infrastructure as referred to in paragraph (1) letter b, is for the fulfillment of service standards;
The provision of facilities and infrastructure by the Regional Government is carried out in stages adjusted to the financial capacity of the Region.

Article 2
The Protection of Women and Children is carried out with due regard to religion, customs, social culture of the Community by prioritizing the basic principles of women's rights and children's rights.
The basic principles of Protection of women's rights and children's rights as referred to in paragraph (1) include: non-discrimination;
the best interests of Women and Children;
the right to life, survival, and development;
respect for the opinion of Children;
legal certainty (Protection of victims' rights);
local wisdom;
justice and gender equality;
transparency;
accountability; and sustainability.

Article 26
(1) 	The Regional Government implements Integrated Services for Women and Children victims of acts of Violence through activities:
a. 	Complaint services;
b. 	Health services;
c. 	counseling;
d. 	spiritual guidance;
e. 	Social Rehabilitation services;
f. 	Legal aid and assistance services; and/or
g. 	repatriation and Reintegration.
(2) 	Services as referred to in paragraph (1) must be supported by facilities in the form of:
a. 	special Service rooms within the police force;
b. 	expert and professional personnel;
c. 	Service centers and safe houses; and/or
d. 	other facilities and infrastructure necessary for victim recovery.
(3) 	The implementation of Services for victims of acts of Violence is carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government together with P2TP2A with other social Institutions.
(4) 	P2TP2A and other social Institutions as referred to in paragraph (3) may receive and send case referrals from other Service units in a networked manner.
(5) 	Integrated Services for victims of acts of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) through paragraph (4) are implemented in accordance with Standard Operating Procedures.

Article 1
In this Regional Regulation, what is meant by: Region is North Lombok Regency;
Regional Government is the Regent and Regional Apparatus as elements of the Regional Government administration;
Regent is the Regent of North Lombok;
Regional Apparatus Work Unit hereinafter abbreviated as SKPD is the Regional Apparatus Work Unit within the North Lombok Regency Government;
Implementation of Protection is all actions and service efforts to guarantee and protect the rights of Women and Children organized by the Regional Government and the Community;
Child is a person who has not yet reached the age of 18 (eighteen) years, including a Child who is still in the womb;
Service is immediate activities and actions carried out by Professional personnel in accordance with their respective professions in the form of counseling, therapy and advocacy for strengthening and recovery;
Assistance is activities and actions carried out by Assistants during the service process;
Assistant is a person or representative from an Institution who has the expertise to provide Assistance/social worker who has professional competence in their field;
Institution is a Community non-governmental organization (NGO) that provides Assistance;
Supervision is a monitoring activity process carried out systematically on the entire Implementation of Protection of legal aid for Children and Women;
Community is individuals, families, groups, social organizations and/or community organizations;
Regional Revenue and Expenditure Budget hereinafter abbreviated as APBD is the annual financial plan of the Region established by Regional Regulation;
Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment hereinafter abbreviated as P2TP2A, is an empowerment and Protection service for Women and Children established by the Government that is Community-based;
Violence is any act against a Child that results in misery or suffering physically, psychologically, sexually, and/or neglect, including threats to commit acts, coercion, or unlawful deprivation of liberty;
Women victims of Violence are Women who experience actions that result in misery or suffering physically, sexually, economically or psychologically, including threats of certain actions, coercion or arbitrary deprivation of liberty, whether occurring in the public sphere or in private life;
Child victims of Violence are Children who experience actions that result in misery or suffering physically, mentally, sexually, psychologically or neglect that threatens life, body and degrades human dignity;
Children in emergency situations referred to are Children who become refugees, Children victims of riots and unrest, Children victims of disasters and Children in conflict situations;
Children in disaster situations are natural disasters, fire disasters and riots;
Complaint handling is a series of actions carried out by integrated service providers to follow up on reports of acts of Violence against Women and Children submitted by victims, families or the Community;
Social rehabilitation is a service aimed at restoring and developing the ability of a person experiencing social dysfunction so that they can carry out their social functions properly;
Social reintegration is an effort to reunite victims with family, substitute family, or Community that can provide Protection and fulfillment of needs for victims;
Integrated service unit or abbreviated as UPT is a unified unit that carries out integrated service functions for Women and Children victims of Violence;
Safe house is a temporary shelter that aims to provide Protection and a sense of security to victims of Violence;
Child Protection Institution or abbreviated as LPA is an Independent Institution in the field of Child Protection and fulfillment of Children's rights that is Community-based;
North Lombok Regency Integrated Service Center or abbreviated as PPT KLU is a form of integrated service delivery based on community health centers to handle victims of Violence against Women and Children which includes medical, medicolegal, and psychosocial services.

Article 24
(1) 	Regional Government conducts prevention of Violence against Women and Children by means of:
a. 	socializing laws and regulations;
b. 	providing counseling/guidance;
c. 	providing education on the dangers of domestic Violence;
d. 	conducting seminars/workshops or the like;
e. 	establishing work networks in efforts to prevent Violence;
f. 	conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of Violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
g. 	establishing a Violence prevention system, mapping of locations or areas prone to occurrence of Violence; and
h. 	increasing Community awareness in behaving in accordance with religious norms and morality.
(2) 	In addition to Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) must be implemented by:
a. 	family and/or closest relatives;
b. 	Community;
c. 	educational institutions;
d. 	health institutions;
e. 	social Community institutions; and
f. 	business sector and other institutions.

