Article 19
(1) Regional Government plays a role in facilitating the handling of Children in conflict with the law.
(2) the handling of Children in conflict with the law as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:
a. capacity building for government apparatus, social workers and the Community;
b. improving coordination with law enforcement apparatus;
c. provision of supporting facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of the juvenile criminal justice system;
d. development of effective methods through information support, facilities and positive activities as well as taking immediate action on gaps that encourage Children and/or groups of Children to commit legal violations;
e. provision and delivery of legal and psychosocial assistance services in realizing restorative justice and diversion processes for Children in conflict with the law;
f. encouraging paradigm shifts in the Community towards Children in conflict with the law; and
g. developing diversion mechanisms for Children in conflict with the law in accordance with applicable laws and regulations.
(3) Related SKPD with authority over social affairs and education shall organize social Rehabilitation and education for Children in conflict with the law in the form of:
a. provision of safe houses;
b. psychosocial Rehabilitation;
c. mental spiritual Rehabilitation;
d. fulfillment of the right to education; and
e. social Reintegration.

Article 11
Every Child has the right to:
a. 	obtain education and teaching in accordance with age level, physical and mental condition, intelligence as well as interests and talents;
b. 	live, grow, develop and participate properly in accordance with human dignity and worth, as well as receive Protection from acts of Violence, exploitation, discrimination and neglect;
c. 	have their needs fulfilled by the family;
d. 	receive religious guidance;
e. 	obtain their identity; and
f. 	obtain other rights in accordance with human dignity and based on the provisions of laws and regulations.
